{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwCkP3qEPMtthX85wXMQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L4WyJo9f7C8K2isMXpEUHm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='paper.tex'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,(s.count(a),a[:60])\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"yet historical score matrices suggest that benchmarks are strongly redundant.\",\"yet benchmarks may be substantially redundant, so a few runs might carry information about the rest.\")\nrep(\"the sealed run used one member of this family (the described pair or its latent-skill extension, which the available evidence cannot tell apart)\",\"the identity of the exact source tree evaluated in the sealed run is not established by the retained artifacts, and we presume it is the development-selected pair or its latent-skill extension\")\nrep(\"\\\\citet{Perlitz2024BenchBench} show that conclusions about benchmark agreement depend strongly on methodological choices such as the reference set and the correlation measure; we therefore define the target, the held-out split and the aggregation explicitly rather than relying on a correlation summary.\",\"Agreement analyses across benchmarks \\\\citep{Perlitz2024BenchBench} bear on how related benchmark scores are; here the target, the held-out split and the aggregation are defined explicitly.\")\nrep(\"The sealed evaluation ran either this pair or its latent-skill extension (below); the two have identical development scores, the recorded hash of the evaluated source tree matches neither retained source copy, and the available evidence cannot say which ran.\",\"The sealed evaluation presumably ran this pair or its latent-skill extension (below), which have identical development scores; no artifact records which source tree was evaluated, so this identity is not established.\")\nrep(\"the sealed run used either this pair or its latent-skill extension (Section~\\\\ref{sec:variants}).\",\"the identity of the sealed-evaluated source tree is not established (presumably this pair or its latent-skill extension, Section~\\\\ref{sec:variants}).\")\nrep(\"Several steps are guarded by wall-clock budgets (candidate evaluation after 70 s, full tuning after 150 s, stacking after 210 s), so on slow hardware the method degrades to the Gaussian-only model.\",\"In the proposed-pair source copy, which is not verified as the sealed-evaluated tree, wall-clock guards skip optional selector candidates after 70 s, fall back to a smaller tuning grid after 150 s, and skip stacking (leaving the Gaussian-only model) after 210 s; the timing above is a property of the sealed run and may not transfer to that copy.\")\nrep(\"scales differ (accuracies, win rates, F1).\",\"metric types differ (accuracy-type, F1, exact-match and BLEU-type metrics).\")\nrep(\"Missingness in leaderboards is not random (strong models are run on more benchmarks), which violates the usual missing-at-random assumption of EM-based imputation \\\\citep{Rubin1976Inference}.\",\"If leaderboard missingness correlates with model strength, the missing-at-random assumption of EM-based imputation \\\\citep{Rubin1976Inference} may fail; we did not test this.\")\nrep(\"Leaderboard missingness is related to model strength and recency; selected benchmarks that are well covered in the history may be missing for new models.\",\"If leaderboard missingness depends on model strength or recency, benchmarks selected for a new model may be sparsely covered in the history; we did not analyse missingness.\")\nrep(\"a handful of well-covered benchmarks and a reasonable imputer already remove\",\"a handful of benchmarks and a reasonable imputer already removed\")\nrep(\"(one member of it, not identifiable from the retained evidence)\",\"(the exact evaluated source tree is not established by the retained artifacts)\")\nrep(\"but no artifact records which of the two tied configurations the sealed run used or that it was run only once;\",\"but no artifact records which of the two tied configurations the sealed run used or that it was run only once, and the identity of the sealed-evaluated tree is not established;\")\nrep(\"we were not able to match this hash to a single source directory, and the tie above means\",\"no hash-comparison artifact is available, so the identity of the evaluated tree is not established, and the tie above means\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nsed -n 207p paper.tex | cut -c1-500; sed -n 248,270p paper.tex | grep -n -i 'guard'"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1698,"cache_read_input_tokens":55968,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1698},"output_tokens":22,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb371e10-197a-4f15-ac67-4967a43d2078","uuid":"fef76dbe-0e7b-4653-bb81-79dc8fd29aa2","timestamp":"2026-11-11T13:16:10.464Z","request_id":"req_011CgwCkNWM4mfdcZLoDdZTm"}
